  "headline": "Westpac's headline Expense to income ratio, ex Notable Items, rose 275 bps (2.75 ppt) to 53.04% in FY25 from 50.29% in FY24 (ev-1, ev-36); the narrative rounds it to \"53.0%, up from 50.3%\" (ev-7). This is negative jaws: net operating income ex Notable Items grew 3% to $22,464m (from $21,763m) while operating expenses grew 9% to $11,916m (from $10,944m) (ev-43, ev-44, ev-39, ev-40). Pre-provision profit ex Notable Items fell 3% to $10,548m (ev-47, ev-42). Expenses included a $273m Fit for Growth restructuring charge taken in 2H25; excluding it, expenses grew 6% (ev-45, ev-41) — still double income growth, so the ratio would have risen even without it. There are no expense-side Notable Items in either year (ev-2), so the statutory expense/income framing gives the same $11,916m vs $10,944m numerator (ev-4); the only basis difference is income Notable Items (ev-5).",
